Package: pve-update-manager
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: pve-update-manager <pve-update-manager@localhost>
License: AGPL-3+
Depends: pve-manager (>= 9.0), pve-container, libpve-common-perl, perl
Description: Update Manager tab for Proxmox VE containers and nodes
 Adds an "Update Manager" tab to every LXC container, to every node and to the
 datacenter in the Proxmox VE web interface.
 .
 The container tab is a text box: the update commands for that container are
 written by hand, stored under /etc/pve/pve-update-manager/, and run inside the
 container by pressing Update. Nothing is generated.
 .
 The node and datacenter tabs list the hosts and every container. Tick the ones
 that should be updated and they all start at once, each in its own Proxmox
 task, with its own log and its own recorded state - which the row then shows.
 The datacenter tab spans the whole cluster, so several servers update at the
 same time.
 .
 A node can also run its updates on a timer: the Schedule window sets the
 interval, which targets are included, and whether they run at the same time or
 one after another (one after another by default).
 .
 The integration is four one-line edits to files owned by pve-manager (a script
 tag in index.html.tpl and a require in pvedaemon, pveproxy and pvesh). They are
 re-applied automatically after a pve-manager upgrade by a dpkg trigger, and
 removed again when this package is.
